hey are big.**\n   - This means that if someone is furry, they are also big.\n\n10. **Round people are furry.**\n    - This means that if someone is round, they are also furry.\n\nNow, let\'s use these rules to determine if Harry is green:\n\n- We know Harry is smart and kind (from rule 4 and 3).\n- From rule 8, since Harry is smart and kind, he must be big.\n- From rule 9, since Harry is big, he must be furry.\n- From rule 10, since Harry is furry, he must be round.\n- From rule 7, since Harry is round, he must be quiet.\n- From rule 6, since Harry is quiet and furry, he must be smart.\n- From rule 5, since Harry is smart, he must be kind.\n- From rule 1, we know that Dave is big, quiet, and round.\n- From rule 2, since Dave is big, he is also kind.\n- From rule 3, since Dave is quiet and round, he is also kind.\n- From rule 4, since Dave is kind, he is also smart.\n- From rule 5, since Dave is smart, he is also kind.\n- From rule 6, since Dave is quiet and furry, he is also smart.\n- From rule 7, since Dave is quiet, he is also furry.\n- From rule 8, since Dave is furry, he is also big.\n- From rule 9, since Dave is big, he is also quiet.\n- From rule 10, since Dave is quiet, he is also round.\n\nSince all the information about Dave applies to Harry, and we have no information that contradicts Harry being green, we cannot determine if Harry is green based on the given information. Therefore, the statement "Harry is green" is unknown.\n\n<｜User｜>The statement "Harry is green" is unknown based on the given information.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
